# Controls what rsconnect (and Posit Publisher, which uses the same
# mechanism) bundles for deployment. One name per line, matched exactly
# against each directory's own listing: no globs, no trailing slashes, no
# regex. List the top-level name of anything that should not ship, and its
# whole subtree is pruned before the bundler ever looks inside it.
#
# .git, .gitignore, renv, rsconnect, node_modules, .Rproj.user and .Rhistory
# are already excluded by rsconnect itself and do not need an entry here.

# CI and repo tooling: no runtime purpose on the server.
.github
.gitattributes
.lintr
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.Rbuildignore
air.toml

# Sources renv/activate.R, which rsconnect already strips out with the rest
# of renv/. Connect restores the library from renv.lock in the manifest, not
# by running this file.
.Rprofile

# Local deployment records and Posit Publisher config: account name, deploy
# history, and (right now) a failed-deploy error message. Bundling these
# would also be circular.
.posit
rsconnect

# Test suite: exercises the Shiny-free logic layer against a fixture, not
# needed to serve the app.
tests

# Catalog build scripts and their scratch output. The app only reads the
# finished snapshot in data/. The scratch directories alone can hold
# hundreds of intermediate .rds files from an interrupted build.
data-raw

# Design notes and local working docs (docs/local/ is gitignored but may
# still exist on disk), not part of the running app.
docs

# Secrets, in case one exists locally but was never committed.
.Renviron
.env

# Leftover from the React front end explored early on; harmless if absent.
node_modules
.vite
